  corn or bean crops or they actually  sometimes get  threatened by cartel groups that require  that they grow them  on their on their plots  mexico production of heroin waxes and  wanes but  at its height there is a huge demand  from the cartels or acetic anhydride  because that's really the only  ingredient missing for them they have  the farmers producing their poppy for  them so  they just need to get a hold of some  jugs of  the chemical and then they're ready to  go  these chemical labs all over poppy  producing regions some of them get  seized by the government and then the  government snaps photos of them  sends them to the media the media puts  them up on their websites and with a  simple google search you can  see what these labs look like so i'm  scouring google looking for  chemical labs and and busts by the army  and i see a bunch of them and they  normally have  a lot of unmarked blue barrels or  unmarked bottles of chemicals  but i came upon one photo where i  actually saw there was a label and the  label read jt baker  i went through more searches and i saw  it on another photo and and  jt baker just kept popping up as one of  the only labels that you could actually  see  on the chemical in these lab busts so we  realized okay something's happening here  so jt baker was a century-old american  brand  that had this really good worldwide  reputation  for its purity and its purity and  control of its production  was a huge part of its marketing to  chemist at universities to chemists in  the in the pharmaceutical industry who  use it in r  d research and development labs it had  been bought the brand in august of 2010  by a company uh that became known as  aventur  from discovery to delivery scientists  and research professionals worldwide  trust avon tour they really had a strong  presence in the lab chemical market  worldwide  but especially in the americas their  operation in mexico  was a significant player for them in the  industry  [Music]  so as 